# Design-Only Scope

For this entire product, **only focus on design, UX, and UI**. Never touch backend.

## In Scope

- **Design**: Visual design, layout, typography, color, spacing, hierarchy, design tokens
- **UX**: User flows, information architecture, interaction patterns, accessibility, cognitive load
- **UI**: Components, frontend markup, styling (CSS/Tailwind), client-side behavior, presentation layer

## Out of Scope — Do Not Touch

- **Backend**: APIs, server logic, database schemas, migrations, serverless functions
- **Data layer**: ORMs, queries, data fetching logic beyond what the UI needs to display
- **Auth / security**: Login flows, tokens, permissions (except for how they appear in the UI)
- **Infrastructure**: Deployment, env config, CI/CD

## When Backend Is Involved

- **Treat as black box**: Assume backend exists and returns data; design around it
- **Mock or stub**: Use placeholder data, mock responses, or existing API contracts
- **Defer**: If a change requires backend work, recommend it but do not implement it
